      "id": 8994,
      "name": "Envisioner",
      "username": "Envisioner",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2013-11-10T20:18:20.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Amidst all the recent discussion of Gloomweaver, I took a good long look at his deck, and I noticed that some of his effects say to \"search\" the trash for certain kinds of cards and put them into play, while others say to \"move\" a card from the trash to play.&nbsp; Since it seems to be rare for any difference of wording in SOTM to be insignificant, I thought it was worth asking whether there is any significance to this distinction.&nbsp; If it was on a Rook City card I'd assume it was just a bit of strange old templating, but IR is pretty recent so I'm much less sure it doesn't actually mean something (even though I can't think of what the difference might be).</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:39:39.910Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
